Week 13 slowdown diagnosis, final. Local scratch Compose project flashsale-diag, all services pinned to two CPU cores except the u- points, 60 s open-loop load after a warm-up load (except e-c2-cold). No AWS.
Set 1: clean clone of 29eefa4, unmodified code. Set 2: ecea5cf plus the uncommitted consumer concurrency option (8 files, handlers not yet concurrency-safe). Set 3: ecea5cf plus the option and the concurrency-safe handlers (9 files). The code changes are not committed.
Values are repeat1/repeat2. Local absolute numbers are not EC2 numbers: compare points within one set. Possibly disturbed by host load: low-all-rep2-25rps-rep1 (build) and st120-all-100rps-rep1 (unit tests).
The Docker restart at about 12:44 UTC killed bd5000-all-100rps-rep1 before it saved; it was rerun from the start.
counters come from Order and Inventory only, so retries reads 0 (the Worker was not scraped). dlq is the queue depth at the end of the run. oc = Order Service consumer concurrency, ic = Inventory consumer concurrency, st = reconciliation StuckTimeoutSeconds, bd = queue bound.

